  "nl_text": "The rschema_0248 database is designed to manage user interactions and activities within a platform. It contains nine tables: User, Article, Book, Activity, Video_Interview, User_Comments, Book_Recommendation, Activity_Lottery, and User_Activity_Participation. The User table stores information about each registered user, including their username, password, role, and registration and last login times, with a unique identifier for each user. The Article table holds details about published articles, such as the title, author, content, and publication time. The Book table contains information about books, including the title, author, and description. The Activity table stores details about various activities, including their names, descriptions, and times. The Video_Interview table stores information about video interviews, including the title, publication time, and link. The User_Comments table links users to articles they have commented on, with a composite primary key of user and article IDs, referencing the User and Article tables respectively. The Book_Recommendation table stores recommendations made by users for books, with a composite primary key of book and recommender IDs, referencing the Book and User tables. The Activity_Lottery table stores information about winners of activities, with a composite primary key of activity and winner IDs, referencing the Activity and User tables. The User_Activity_Participation table tracks user participation in activities, with a composite primary key of user and activity IDs, referencing the User and Activity tables. Each of these tables is designed to maintain data integrity through primary keys, composite keys, and foreign keys that enforce relationships between tables, ensuring that data remains consistent and accurate.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a user-article sharing forum with the following features:\n1.User Interaction Features:\nEach user has a unique User ID, Username, Password, Registration Time, Last Login Time, and Role.\nA user can participate in multiple activities, engage in video interviews, and comment or recommend books and articles.\n2.Content Management:\nThe system manages several books and articles.\nBook Information: Each book has a Book ID, Title, Author, and Description.\nArticle Information: Each article has an Article ID, Title, Content, Author, and Publish Time.\nActivity Information: Each activity has an Activity ID, Activity Name, Activity Time, and Description.\nVideo Interview Information: Each video interview has a Video ID, Title, Video Link, and Publish Time.\n3.Activity Management:\nThe system can organize source code reading activities, record activity names, times, and descriptions.\nUsers can participate in multiple activities.\nThe system also handles lottery activities, recording winner information and awarding gifts.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0248.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0248\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Activity` (\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `activity_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`activity_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Video_Interview` (\n  `video_interview_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `link` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`video_interview_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Comments` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `Article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Book_Recommendation` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recommender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `recommender_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `Book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recommender_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Activity_Lottery` (\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`activity_id`, `winner_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `Activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winner_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Activity_Participation` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `activity_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `Activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
